read: [
{t:"For many young Vietnamese, the 'side hustle' has become a normal part of life. Linh, a 27-year-old accountant, has been selling handmade candles online for two years. 'I started it because I wanted to save for a house,' she explains. 'At first, I only sold a few candles a month, but now I have regular customers all over the country.' However, running a business alongside a full-time job is not easy. Linh often works until midnight, and she admits that she rarely has time to see her friends. 'If I could choose again, I would still do it,' she says, 'but I wish I had planned my time better from the beginning.'",q:["Why did Linh start her business?|To save for a house|Because she lost her job|To help her friends","How has her business changed?|She now has regular customers nationwide|She has opened a shop in her hometown|She now sells candles only to her friends","What is a disadvantage mentioned?|She rarely sees her friends|She earns very little|Customers often complain","What does Linh regret?|Not planning her time better|Starting the business|Becoming an accountant"]},
{t:"A recent survey of 2,000 parents found that children aged 8 to 12 spend an average of four hours a day in front of screens, excluding schoolwork. Doctors warn that too much screen time can lead to poor sleep and less physical activity. However, the survey also showed that children who used screens for creative activities, such as making videos or learning to code, tended to have better problem-solving skills. Experts therefore suggest that parents should focus not only on how long children use screens, but also on what they use them for.",q:["How much time do children spend on screens daily?|About four hours|About two hours|About eight hours","Which problem is mentioned by doctors?|Poor sleep|Bad eyesight|Lower grades","Which children had better problem-solving skills?|Those using screens creatively|Those who spent the least time on screens|Those who played games","What do experts suggest?|Looking at what screens are used for|Banning all screens on school nights|Limiting screen time to two hours a day"]},
{t:"Dear Sir or Madam,\nI am writing to complain about the hotel room I stayed in from June 10 to 12. When I booked, the website said that the room had an ocean view and that breakfast was included. However, my room faced the parking lot, and I was asked to pay extra for breakfast. When I spoke to the receptionist, she said that the hotel was full and that nothing could be done. I would therefore like a partial refund for the difference in price. I look forward to your reply.\nSincerely,\nPham Van Duc",q:["What did the website promise?|An ocean view and free breakfast|A free upgrade to a larger room|Free airport transfers and parking","What was the problem with the room?|It faced the parking lot|It was too small for two people|It was dirty","What did the receptionist say?|The hotel was full|Breakfast was free|The manager would call","What does Duc want?|A partial refund|A new room next year|A free dinner"]}],
